---
layout: layouts/tool.njk
toolSlug: gold-calculator
title: "Gold Calculator: Price by Tola, Gram & Karat"
description: "Work out the price of gold by tola, gram, masha or ratti for 24K, 22K, 21K or 18K from today's rate, with making charges and rates per tola and per gram."
permalink: /tools/gold-calculator/
h1: "Gold Calculator: Price by Tola, Gram & Karat"
extraCss: "/tools/gold-calculator/style.css"
quickAnswer: "Gold price = weight in grams × (karat ÷ 24) × the rate of pure gold per gram. At Rs 400,000 per tola for 24K, 2 tola of 22K gold is worth Rs 733,333.33 and 10 grams of 24K is Rs 342,941.30, before making charges. One tola is 11.6638038 grams."
formula:
  title: "Gold Price Formula"
  expression: "Gold value = Weight (g) × (Item karat ÷ 24) × Pure gold rate per gram"
  explanation: "First turn the rate you were quoted into the price of one gram of pure (24K) gold: divide by the grams in the rate's unit (11.6638038 for a tola, 10 for 10 grams) and divide by the purity of the rate's karat. Then multiply by the item's weight in grams and its purity. Making charges are added on top, either as a percentage of the gold value or as a fixed amount per gram."
  variables:
    - name: "Weight (g)"
      description: "The item's weight converted to grams: 1 tola = 11.6638038 g, 1 masha = 1/12 tola, 1 ratti = 1/8 masha."
    - name: "Karat ÷ 24"
      description: "Purity as a fraction: 22K = 22/24 = 91.7%, 21K = 87.5%, 18K = 75%."
    - name: "Pure gold rate per gram"
      description: "The 24K price of one gram, worked out from the rate you entered."
workedExamples:
  - title: "2 tola of 22K at Rs 400,000 per tola (24K)"
    inputs:
      - "Rate: Rs 400,000 per tola for 24K"
      - "Weight: 2 tola"
      - "Item karat: 22K"
    steps:
      - "22K purity: 22 ÷ 24 = 0.916667"
      - "Gold value: 2 × 400,000 × 0.916667 = 733,333.33"
    result: "Rs 733,333.33 (22K rate: Rs 366,666.67 per tola)"
    link: "/tools/gold-calculator/?rate=400000&per=tola&ratek=24&weight=2&unit=tola&karat=22&cur=PKR#tool"
  - title: "10 grams of 24K and 21K"
    inputs:
      - "Rate: Rs 400,000 per tola for 24K"
      - "Weight: 10 g"
    steps:
      - "24K rate per gram: 400,000 ÷ 11.6638038 = 34,294.13"
      - "10 g of 24K: 10 × 34,294.13 = Rs 342,941.30"
      - "10 g of 21K: 10 × (21 ÷ 24) × 34,294.13 = Rs 300,073.63"
    result: "Rs 342,941.30 for 24K, Rs 300,073.63 for 21K"
    link: "/tools/gold-calculator/?rate=400000&per=tola&ratek=24&weight=10&unit=gram&karat=21&cur=PKR#tool"
  - title: "1 masha of 24K"
    inputs:
      - "Rate: Rs 400,000 per tola for 24K"
      - "Weight: 1 masha (1/12 tola)"
    steps:
      - "1 masha = 11.6638038 ÷ 12 = 0.9719836 g"
      - "Value: 400,000 ÷ 12 = 33,333.33"
    result: "Rs 33,333.33"
    link: "/tools/gold-calculator/?rate=400000&per=tola&ratek=24&weight=1&unit=masha&karat=24&cur=PKR#tool"
  - title: "10 grams of 22K with Rs 500 per gram making"
    inputs:
      - "Rate: Rs 400,000 per tola for 24K"
      - "Weight: 10 g, 22K"
      - "Making charges: Rs 500 per gram"
    steps:
      - "Gold value: 10 × (22 ÷ 24) × 34,294.13 = Rs 314,362.86"
      - "Making charges: 10 × 500 = Rs 5,000"
      - "Total: 314,362.86 + 5,000 = Rs 319,362.86"
    result: "Rs 319,362.86 including making charges"
    link: "/tools/gold-calculator/?rate=400000&per=tola&ratek=24&weight=10&unit=gram&karat=22&making=perGram&mv=500&cur=PKR#tool"
commonMistakes:
  - title: "Using a 24K rate for 22K or 21K jewellery"
    description: "Jewellery is rarely 24K. If the rate you were given is for 24K and the item is 22K, the gold in it is only 22/24 of its weight. Paying the 24K rate for 22K jewellery overpays by about 9%."
  - title: "Treating a tola as 10 grams"
    description: "A tola is 11.6638038 grams, not 10. Rates quoted per tola and per 10 grams are different numbers, so check which one you have before comparing shops."
  - title: "Mixing up the rate's karat"
    description: "Some shops quote a 22K rate, others a 24K rate. Choose the karat the rate is for, then the karat of the item; the calculator scales between them."
  - title: "Ignoring making charges and kaat"
    description: "The price you pay for jewellery includes making charges, and when you sell or exchange it a jeweller may deduct kaat (a wastage or impurity deduction). The pure gold value is only part of the shop's price."
  - title: "Counting stone weight as gold"
    description: "If a piece has stones, beads or lacquer, their weight is not gold. Ask for the net gold weight before working out its value."
faqs:
  - q: "How do I calculate the price of gold per tola?"
    a: "Multiply the number of tola by the rate per tola for the karat you are buying. If your rate is for 24K and the item is 22K, multiply by 22 ÷ 24 as well. At Rs 400,000 per tola for 24K, 2 tola of 22K is 2 × 400,000 × 22/24 = Rs 733,333.33."
  - q: "How many grams are in one tola?"
    a: "One tola is 11.6638038 grams. It is defined as 180 grains, and a grain is 64.79891 milligrams."
  - q: "How many masha and ratti are in one tola?"
    a: "One tola is 12 masha, and one masha is 8 ratti, so one tola is 96 ratti. One masha is about 0.972 grams and one ratti about 0.1215 grams."
  - q: "How do I calculate the 22K gold price from the 24K rate?"
    a: "Multiply the 24K rate by 22 ÷ 24, which is about 0.9167. A 24K rate of Rs 400,000 per tola is Rs 366,666.67 per tola for 22K. For 21K multiply by 21 ÷ 24 (0.875), and for 18K by 18 ÷ 24 (0.75)."
  - q: "What is the difference between 22K and 21K gold?"
    a: "22K gold is about 91.7% pure gold and 21K is 87.5%, so 21K contains less gold per gram and is worth less at the same weight. The rest is other metals that make the jewellery harder."
  - q: "Why is the jeweller's price higher than this calculator?"
    a: "Shops add making charges for the work, may add wastage, and may round the rate. The calculator shows the gold value and the making charges separately, so you can compare what part of a quote is for the gold itself."
  - q: "What is kaat in gold?"
    a: "Kaat is a deduction a jeweller makes when buying back or exchanging gold, to allow for impurity, wastage or solder in the piece. The amount varies between shops, so ask how much kaat will be deducted before you sell."
  - q: "Where can I find today's gold rate?"
    a: "Take the day's rate from your local sarafa association or your jeweller. This calculator does not fetch live prices; type the rate you were quoted and choose its unit and karat."
